# held/weapons/staff: the plain staff (art weapon 4, `held staff.plain`): 30 px of ash drawn as the civil staff is (held/civil/staff: a 1 px lit line in a dark outline, 3 px across), a dark butt and the civil staff head (a brass collar, a dark claw and a 3 x 3 orb in the accent colour, its lit pixel the gem G: glowing at T5-T6), so the swing matches the carry. Origin = the right fist 9 px from the foot; the left fist takes the staff 6-8 px further up. The carry (upright, the fist on the shaft) is the civil staff drawing, copied below (P2c wave 2, WEAPONS). STYLE_P2 11 / 25.7; P2C_CONTRACTS 4: the library weapon on the grip,
# a000..a337 = degrees counter-clockwise from screen-right, drawn once (D) for every facing; origin = the grip point
# under the main fist (the hand is drawn over the grip); `mark tip` at the far end. Drafted with the area's stepper (exact
# 1:0, 2:1, 1:1 and 1:2 runs, the top-left light by rule: a 2 px band's upper / left line lit) and hand-cleaned at 12x.
# Finish regions (contracts 3b): R the ferrule and head, G the glow pixel.
# (wave 2 r4, D5) carryR / carryL are the upright carry (the a090 drawing, the fist on the haft, as the spear's side carry) (facing right the haft 1 px ahead of the grip, clear of the face: B11 W7); runcarry keeps the one-step tilt. They serve the staff carry clip (`family staff when staff`: armR guard D/U, sp_carry R/L, which mark `grip`).
use person
body adult
role held staff.plain
layer held
anchor grip
keys held
tags anyfacing
